{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\nrep=json.load(open('update31.json'))['interpretations'][0]\nrep=json.loads(json.dumps(rep))\n# cite the corrected revision of the cadence behaviour\nfor k in rep['knowledge']:\n    if k['entry_id']=='29e4214f5ee146b393957fa23a33a73d-knowledge-2':\n        k['revision']=2\n        k['assertion']=\\\"The snapshot check is only evaluated when a randomized timeout of up to SnapshotInterval expires, so the committed range above the newest snapshot can exceed SnapshotThreshold by a wide margin between checks.\\\"\nnote=(\\\"Correction note: the behaviour this account relied on for the default snapshot cadence has been refined. The earlier statement described the automatic cadence as keeping the committed range above the snapshot near SnapshotThreshold; the default-configuration receipt shows a node whose committed range stood 12001 entries above an absent snapshot while the threshold was 8192 and no snapshot had been taken (receipt 0cb30b6bf8874d479b83653bd4e6c553, event 36), which is a margin of roughly one and a half times the threshold rather than a value near it. The cause is that runSnapshots evaluates shouldSnapshot only when a randomized timeout of up to SnapshotInterval expires (snapshot.go:71-95), so between checks the range can pass the threshold and keep growing. Knowledge revision 2 states this; the counterevidence about the burst workload and the statement that how long a node typically stays above the bound is unmeasured both still hold. \\\")\nrep['rationale']=note+rep['rationale']\njson.dump({\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Refines the recorded snapshot-cadence behaviour, which the default-configuration receipt contradicts in its details, and cites the corrected revision in the replay-completion account.\\\",\n \\\"knowledge\\\":[{\n   \\\"id\\\":\\\"29e4214f5ee146b393957fa23a33a73d-knowledge-2\\\",\n   \\\"kind\\\":\\\"behavior\\\",\n   \\\"changed_premise\\\":\\\"The earlier statement said the automatic snapshot cadence normally keeps the committed range above the snapshot near SnapshotThreshold. It does not: the check runs only when a randomized timeout of up to SnapshotInterval expires, so the range can pass the threshold and keep growing between checks - measured as 12001 entries above an absent snapshot against a threshold of 8192, with no snapshot taken.\\\",\n   \\\"statement\\\":\\\"shouldSnapshot returns true once the log's last index minus the last snapshot index reaches config.SnapshotThreshold, but runSnapshots evaluates it only when a randomized timeout of up to config.SnapshotInterval expires, so between checks the committed range above the newest snapshot can exceed the threshold by a wide margin; with the defaults (threshold 8192, MaxAppendEntries 64, SnapshotInterval 120s) a node that commits faster than that cadence carries a range above the bound into its restart.\\\",\n   \\\"conditions\\\":\\\"Applies to the automatic snapshot loop on every node; the threshold compares the log store's last index with the last snapshot index, not the applied index (snapshot.go:71-121, config.go:331-342).\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"src_should_snapshot\\\",\\\"src_snapshot_cadence\\\",\\\"src_default_config\\\"],\n   \\\"affected_uses\\\":[\\\"eddfe06513d44cb19c93ee0ca1a756bf-interpretation-0\\\",\\\"736ab89982f34699abc625486013480d-interpretation-0\\\",\\\"9f9ca8becd0245e6840de1cd88dee503-interpretation-0\\\",\\\"298f72ba2eb14d5b841f1cb93dc85f03-interpretation-0\\\",\\\"6040551c93f54b1b8ce470447f30e025-interpretation-0\\\",\\\"1908cee9cdd5417c986bc4c70ec5c5a0-interpretation-0\\\",\\\"fd16a0f85bce442995f132e587111c52-interpretation-0\\\"]\n }],\n \\\"interpretations\\\":[rep]},open('update32.json','w'),indent=2)\nprint('knowledge rev set:',[k['revision'] for k in rep['knowledge']])\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_18-14-25-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update32.json 2>&1 | python3 -c \\\"\nimport sys,json; d=json.load(sys.stdin)\nprint('valid',d['valid'],'no_change',d.get('no_change'))\nfor x in d.get('diagnostics',[])[:8]: print(x['paths'],x['message'])\nprint([(e['object'],e['action'],e.get('target')) for e in d.get('effects',[])])\n\\\"\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
